---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The placeholder, and it says so. W-C replaces the routing here with W1, the public tree page
// that `SCREENS.md` section W1 transcribes and that every share link the iOS app has ever
// produced already points at.
//
// It renders on the server rather than at build time, so that a request to this app proves the
// whole path — adapter, entry, container, port — rather than proving that a file was copied.
const renderedAt = new Date().toISOString();
---

<Base title="Cypress on the web">
  <h1>Cypress on the web</h1>
  <p>
    This app is scaffolding. Nothing here is the product yet: milestone <strong>W-A</strong> builds
    the directory, the CI carve-out and the test harness, and stops there.
  </p>
  <p>
    The public tree page arrives in <strong>W-C</strong>. It is already transcribed in
    <code>docs/distilled/SCREENS.md</code>, and the design that governs this whole round is
    <code>docs/design-proposals/2026-09-10-web-version.md</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Rendered on the server at <time datetime={renderedAt}>{renderedAt}</time>.
  </p>
</Base>
